# A lens on the board's file: `pin` puts a Notice into the file and `posts` gets it back as the Posts the file holds, a
# Notice being a Post. Building the Notice runs its constructor, which runs Post's on it (`super(text)`): that makes no
# value of its own, it sets up the Notice being built. The route of the exported class is its constructor and its
# public methods, each called by its caller and run on the caller's Board; what the constructor builds goes back to
# that caller.

route club.files.Board
step Board()/Board()
step Board()/Board.pin
step Board()/Board.posts
step Board()/Board.posts/Notice()
known #146 step Board()/Board.posts/Notice()/Post()           # super(text) runs Post's constructor

line entry > Board()/Board() call
line entry > Board()/Board.pin call
line entry > Board()/Board.posts call
line Board()/Board() > Board@Board()/Board() value
known #74 line Board > Board()/Board.pin value   # the caller's instance: every method runs on it
known #74 line Board > Board()/Board.posts/parse value   # `readFileSync(this.path, ..)` in what `parse` is handed
known #127 line Notice·notice > Board()/Board.pin value          # #127
line Board()/Board.pin > Disk(Board.path) own
line Disk(Board.path) > Board()/Board.posts own
line Board()/Board.posts/Notice() > Notice@Board()/Board.posts/Notice() value
line Notice@Board()/Board.posts/Notice() > Board()/Board.posts value
line Board()/Board.posts > Post@Board()/Board.posts value

home Board@Board()/Board() Board()
known #74 home Board Board()
known #127 home Notice·notice Board()
home Notice@Board()/Board.posts/Notice() Board()/Board.posts
home Post@Board()/Board.posts Board()

side entry left
side Disk(Board.path) between

# #127: the parameter of a method the entry calls has lost its name
known #127 extra line Notice > Board()/Board.pin value
known #127 extra home Notice Board()
# the record `posts` parses is a step of its own (a library's operation whose result the body names), and the Notice is
# built from its fields
step Board()/Board.posts/parse
line Board()/Board.posts/parse > _·kept@Board()/Board.posts/parse value
line _·kept@Board()/Board.posts/parse > Board()/Board.posts/Notice() value
home _·kept@Board()/Board.posts/parse Board()/Board.posts

# what the constructor builds goes back to its caller: Atlas runs the methods on it instead of the caller's instance
known #74 extra line Board@Board()/Board() > Board()/Board.pin value
known #74 extra line Board@Board()/Board() > Board()/Board.posts/parse value
